WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
Grass grows in a field.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.240
A rabbit eats the grass.

3
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.370
A fox eats the rabbit.

4
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.650
With every bite, energy passes
one step along the chain.

5
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.190
And none of that energy ever
travels back to the grass.

6
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.700
So where does a food chain's energy
come from in the first place,

7
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.480
and where does it end up?

8
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.940
In this mission, you'll read food webs,
and learn which way the arrows really

9
00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:24.950
point.

10
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.040
Then you'll sort living
things into feeding levels,

11
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.180
from producers up to tertiary consumers.

12
00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.960
Your mission: find out where
a food chain's energy starts,

13
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.210
and where it goes.
